                <head>DR–4. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On September 16, 1958, the Dominican Congress adopted a joint resolution
                    abolishing the resolution of June 18. In telegram 121 from Ciudad Trujillo,
                    September 17, 1958, Ambassador Farland informed the Department of this action.
                    The telegram stated in part, that the action of the Dominican Congress
                    reaffirmed “Gimo Trujillo’s policy of associating the Dominican Republic without
                    vacillation and without reservation to the ‘destiny of the U.S. and to all
                    peoples in the anti-Communist world.’” (739.5–MSP/9–1758) In despatch 150 from
                    Ciudad Trujillo, September 18, 1958, the Embassy forwarded to the Department of
                    State a translation of the joint resolution and also of Dominican Foreign Office
                    note 28105, dated September 17, which accompanied it. (732.5–MSP/91858)</p>
            </div>
